  "Id": 1656,
  "Title": "Sitara-i-Imtiaz for Professor Mohammad Iqbal",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Professor Iqbal works in the department of biological and biomedical sciences at AKU.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The president of Pakistan has conferred the prestigious Sitara-i-Imtiaz on Dr Mohammad Perwaiz Iqbal, a professor in the department of biological and biomedical sciences at AKU. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Dr Iqbal, who holds a PhD from New York University, joined AKU in 1983. An accomplished biological scientist, Dr Iqbal is a recognised authority in the field of protein chemistry and folate metabolism. His research interests include the role of various antimetabolites in cancer, the pharmacokinetics of antifolate drugs, the role of glutathione in imparting drug resistance in cancer cells, and the mechanism by which cytokines (G-CSF and GM-CSF) induce white cell proliferation in cancer patients. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Dr Iqbal is grateful to the University for providing him with the environment that has enabled him to make meaningful contribution to teaching and research."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
